Once upon a time there was a young inexperienced samurai that had the luck
to *FIND* a blessed war hammer named Mjollnir, on a level < 10. Thinking
that this was a *very* good start, he descended a few levels to find two
well furnished shops, a dead brother who had gathered a lot of goodies, and
an altar of A.O. (lawfull). Furthermore, he gained poison resistance without
a decrease in strength and found a pair of speed boots. But then luck changed.
First, the healthy young samurai went blind by an exploding yellow light.
Nothing to worry about, time will cure all wounds. While being blind, the
healthy young samurai was attacked by a monster. When someone is wielding a war
hammer named Mjollnir, this is a very stoopid thing to do: he needed two
strokes to kill the monster. Then the healthy young healty samurai stepped on
the monster, to identify and eat it. He had no reason to fear cockatrices,
because he had never seen them before (in that particular quest) and hadn't
descended that far. Then the poor healty young samurai identified the monster:
it was a member of the dreaded species of cockatrices. He would never again
feel the warmth of the sun, see the eyes of his beloved, or hear the laughter 
of his friends. Instead, he was doomed to stand forever in a indignifying pose,
being pissed upon by stoopid litle dogs.

So, if you visit the dungeons, and happen to find the statue of a healthy young
samurai wielding a war hammer named Mjollnir, seeming to bend to the ground to
touch something, then remember this sad story and pity him.

With grief,

